      "writtenOn": "2021-04-26T03:52:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg,\n\nueventd listens for uevents emitted by the kernel and tries to process them. Since the kset for per-buffer attachment sysfs statistics get created everytime a buffer gets allocated, it causes a measurable perf impact during high resolution video playback. Please find further details in b/186155231. There is no usecase/tool that needs to process the uevents from these sysfs statistics or monitor them on a realtime basis. They are only read during bugreport collection and occasionally by telemetry.",
      "parentUuid": "2e9305a3_f9498de8",
      "revId": "4d745fec0afe0c6ac27a1ce9c3de14cd1a995e5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
