      "writtenOn": "2021-04-26T06:02:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh wow, no, this isn\u0027t going to be ok.\n\nThe kobject create path is NOT a fast path at all.  If this is being called for buffers that are constantly being allocated like this, then the kobject dma-buf code needs to be reworked.  I thought these buffers were created \"once at boot\" and then reused all the time, not created constantly like this.\n\nThis patch would just paper-over the problem here, please do not create/destroy kobject so quickly as that is not a wise idea.",
      "parentUuid": "3d6f3eb7_80f6b461",
